/-! # Coherent modules with zero-dimensional support

Source: Stacks Project, Cohomology of Schemes, Tag 0B3J,
lemma-coherent-support-dimension-0
(blueprint: lem-sfb-coherent-zero-dimensional-support).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

/-- A coherent module on a locally Noetherian scheme whose support has dimension at most
zero is generated by its global sections, has no positive module-sheaf cohomology,
and is zero if its global sections vanish. The evaluation morphism is the coproduct
of the canonical maps `homOfGlobalSection F s : O_X ⟶ F`, indexed by all `s ∈ F(X)`.
Source: Stacks Project, Cohomology of Schemes, Tag 0B3J,
lemma-coherent-support-dimension-0
(blueprint: lem-sfb-coherent-zero-dimensional-support).

Proof:
1. By pqf-lem-coherent-ft-locnoeth, F is quasi-coherent of finite type. Its annihilator
   defines the scheme-theoretic support i : Z → X, with image the nonzero-stalk locus,
   by lem-weil-pbc-scheme-theoretic-support. Thus the dimension bound holds on Z.
2. A closed immersion is locally of finite type, so Z is locally Noetherian
   (lem-weil-pbc-immersion-base-change-lft and pqf-lem-locnoeth-lft). The coherent
   closed-immersion equivalence (lem-weil-pbc-closed-immersion-coherent-equivalence)
   writes F as i_* G for coherent G on Z. By
   lem-sfb-locally-noetherian-zero-dimensional-discrete, Z is discrete.
3. At z ∈ Z, a germ is a section on the open singleton {z}; extend it by zero on
   its open complement. The pushforward-stalk description
   (lem-weil-pbc-closed-pushforward-stalks) supplies every germ of F by a global
   section, and the remaining stalks vanish. Hence the evaluation map is surjective
   on stalks, and is an epimorphism of module sheaves.
4. More generally, extend any section on i⁻¹ U by zero on its open complement in
   i⁻¹ V for U ⊆ V. This proves the underlying abelian sheaf is flasque
   (def-sc-zariski-flasque), without requiring the support to be finite.
5. Apply lem-sc-module-cup-flasque-acyclicity to obtain vanishing of the specified
   module-sheaf cohomology in every positive degree.
6. If the global sections vanish, generation forces every stalk to vanish. A section
   with zero germs is locally zero by def-weil-pbc-module-stalk, hence zero by sheaf
   uniqueness. Thus F is a zero object. This also covers empty support and empty X.
-/
theorem coherent_zero_dimensional_support (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    (F : X.Modules) (hF : RingedSpace.IsCoherent X.toRingedSpace F)
    (hdim : topologicalKrullDim {x : X | ¬ Subsingleton (F.presheaf.stalk x)} ≤ 0) :
    Epi (Sigma.desc (fun s : F.presheaf.obj (op ⊤) ↦ homOfGlobalSection F s)) ∧
      (∀ i : ℕ, 0 < i → IsZero ((RingedSpace.moduleCohomology X.toRingedSpace i).obj F)) ∧
      (Subsingleton (F.presheaf.obj (op ⊤)) → IsZero F) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
